{
    "en": {
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_NAME": "Pathfinder",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Birds of Prey",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_LORE": "\"You bloody idiot, that's not a Red Snubtail, that's a Rosy Quillback rat! You caught the wrong rodent.\"\n\n\"So what? It's got red fur and a stubby tail, I say we just take it and finish the job.\"\n\n\"We've been over this; snubtails mimic quillbacks to deter predators, so you have to check their fur for tiny spines. Also, quillbacks are strict insectivores; that's why I told you not to use the live insect bait, so you wouldn't accidentally attract one. Did you even read the bestiary entries that I showed you?\"\n\n\"So it's got some puny needles on its arse, big deal. We've been chasing after a damn rat for three days now. Besides, our client's just some rich snob looking for a fancy exotic pet to show off in front of their other rich snob friends; they'll never tell the difference. This one's just a tiny bit prickly, they won't mind.\"\n\n\"Did you forget that quillbacks are <i>poisonous</i>, genius? They'll damn well be able to tell the bloody difference when they pet the bugger, then wake up the next morning, paralyzed head to toe. Do you want to earn us a manslaughter charge, you mongrel?\"\n\n\"They're poisonous?\"\n\n\"................... Where are your gloves?\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"I'm finding a new partner.\"\n\n",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_DESCRIPTION": "The Pathfinder is a cunning and evasive skirmisher who fights alongside his robotic falcon, Squall.<color=#CCD3E0>\n\n< ! > You are quite fragile compared to other melee survivors; use your quick feet, long reach, and Squall’s distractions to stay alive.\n\n< ! > Alternate between Fleetfoot and your javelin toss to throw as many javelins as possible, but reserve a skill charge to dodge when necessary.\n\n< ! > Shock Bolas can lock down large groups of enemies, while Rending Talons can deal brutal damage when combined with items that increase your air time.\n\n< ! > Squall is a capable fighter; command him often and prioritize attack speed and critical chance items to help charge the battery.</color>",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_PASSIVE_NAME": "Falconer",
        "KEYWORD_BATTERY": "<style=cKeywordName>Battery</style><style=cSub>Squall has two modes: <color=#FF0000>Attack</color> and <color=#00FF00>Follow</color>. In <color=#FF0000>Attack</color>, the battery rapidly <style=cIsDamage>drains</style>. In <color=#00FF00>Follow</color>, it <style=cIsHealing>regenerates</style> in proportion to <style=cIsUtility>his attack speed</style>.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_PIERCE": "<style=cKeywordName>Piercing</style><style=cSub>Striking with the <style=cIsUtility>tip</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>325% damage</style> and <style=cIsDamage>bypasses armor</style> instead.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_ELECTROCUTE": "<style=cKeywordName>Electrocute</style><style=cSub>Targets have their movement speed reduced by 50% and take <style=cIsDamage>120% damage</style> per second.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_ATTACK": "<style=cKeywordName><color=#FF0000>Attack</color></style><style=cSub>Direct Squall's attention to the target enemy and activate <color=#FF0000>Attack Mode</color>, granting access to machine guns dealing <style=cIsDamage>2x30% damage</style> and a missile launcher dealing <style=cIsDamage>150% damage</style>.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_FOLLOW": "<style=cKeywordName><color=#00FF00>Follow</color></style><style=cSub>Bring Squall back close to you and activate <color=#00FF00>Follow Mode</color>, causing him to stay near you.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_SQUALL_SPECIAL": "<style=cKeywordName><color=#efeb1c>Go for the Throat!</color></style><style=cSub>Order Squall to repeatedly attack the target enemy for <style=cIsDamage>70% damage</style>. Each attack briefly reduces <style=cIsDamage>armor</style> and <style=cIsUtility>regenerates 1%</style> battery, doubled on Critical Hits. This skill can briefly <style=cIsUtility>overcharge</style> the battery.</style>",
        "KEYWORD_UNPOLISHED": "<style=cKeywordName>Unpolished</style><style=cSub>This skill is missing visual and sound effects and is probably buggier than the others.</style>",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "You are accompanied by your robotic falcon, Squall. Squall inherits <style=cIsDamage>most</style> of your items and is immune to damage, but runs on a <style=cIsUtility>battery</style>.",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_DEFAULT_SKIN_NAME": "Default",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_MASTERY_SKIN_NAME": "Headhunter",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_OUTRO_FLAVOR": "..and so they left, as the new kings of the food chain.",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_OUTRO_FAILURE": "..and so they vanished, lost forever to the indifferent wilds.",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_NAME": "Squall",
        "BOGSQUALL_SPECIAL_GOFORTHROAT_NAME": "Go for the Throat!",
        "BOGSQUALL_SPECIAL_GOFORTHROAT_DESCRIPTION": "Order Squall to repeatedly attack the target enemy for <style=cIsDamage>70% damage</style>. Each attack briefly reduces <style=cIsDamage>armor</style> and <style=cIsUtility>regenerates 1%</style> battery, doubled on Critical Hits. This skill can briefly <style=cIsUtility>overcharge</style> the battery.",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_PICKUP": "The Pathfinder's loyal robotic falcon.",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_DESCRIPTION": "A robotic falcon that accompanies Pathfinder. Squall inherits most of Pathfinder's items and <style=cIsUtility>cannot be destroyed</style>.",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires mounted guns and missiles at enemies while in <color=#FF0000>Attack Mode</color>, and repeatedly strikes targets when ordered to <style=cIsDamage>Go for the Throat!</style>.",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_DEFAULT_SKIN_NAME": "Default",
        "BOG_SQUALL_BODY_MASTERY_SKIN_NAME": "Mastery",
        "PRIMARY_THRUST_NAME": "Thrust",
        "PRIMARY_THRUST_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Piercing</style>. Push your spear forward for <style=cIsDamage>250% damage</style>.",
        "SECONDARY_DASH_NAME": "Fleetfoot",
        "SECONDARY_DASH_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Dash</style> a short distance. The next time you use your primary skill, throw an <style=cIsDamage>explosive</style> javelin for <style=cIsDamage>800% damage</style>.",
        "SECONDARY_JAVELIN_NAME": "Explosive Javelin",
        "SECONDARY_JAVELIN_DESCRIPTION": "Throw an <style=cIsDamage>explosive</style> javelin for <style=cIsDamage>800% damage</style>.",
        "UTILITY_SPIN_NAME": "Rending Talons",
        "UTILITY_SPIN_DESCRIPTION": "Rise into the air, spinning rapidly for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>. Upon landing, perform a horizontal sweep for <style=cIsDamage>800% damage</style>.",
        "UTILITY_BOLAS_NAME": "Shock Bolas",
        "UTILITY_BOLAS_DESCRIPTION": "Throw electrically charged bolas that <style=cIsUtility>shock</style> nearby enemies and leave an <style=cIsUtility>electrocuting</style> field for <style=cIsUtility>10 seconds</style>.",
        "SPECIAL_COMMAND_NAME": "Issue Command",
        "SPECIAL_COMMAND_DESCRIPTION": "Prepare a command for Squall. You can issue an <color=#FF0000>Attack</color>, <color=#00FF00>Follow</color>, or <color=#efeb1c>Special</color> command by pressing Primary, Secondary, or Special skill keys respectively.",
        "SPECIAL_COMMAND2_NAME": "Issue Command - Utility Override",
        "SPECIAL_ATTACK_NAME": "Attack",
        "SPECIAL_ATTACK_DESCRIPTION": "Direct Squall's attention to the target enemy and activate <color=#FF0000>Attack Mode</color>, granting access to machine guns dealing <style=cIsDamage>2x30% damage</style> and a missile launcher dealing <style=cIsDamage>150% damage</style>.",
        "SPECIAL_FOLLOW_NAME": "Follow",
        "SPECIAL_FOLLOW_DESCRIPTION": "Bring Squall back close to you and activate <color=#00FF00>Follow Mode</color>, causing him to stay near you.",
        "SPECIAL_CANCEL_NAME": "Cancel Command Mode",
        "SPECIAL_CANCEL_DESCRIPTION": "Cancels Command Mode.",
        "SQUALL_SPECIAL_GOFORTHROAT_NAME": "Go for the Throat!",
        "SQUALL_SPECIAL_GOFORTHROAT_DESCRIPTION": "Order Squall to repeatedly attack the target enemy for <style=cIsDamage>70% damage</style>. Each attack briefly reduces <style=cIsDamage>armor</style> and <style=cIsUtility>regenerates 1%</style> battery, doubled on Critical Hits. This skill can briefly <style=cIsUtility>overcharge</style> the battery.",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_MASTERYUNLOCKABLE_ACHIEVEMENT_NAME": "Pathfinder: Mastery",
        "BOG_PATHFINDER_BODY_MASTERYUNLOCKABLE_ACHIEVEMENT_DESC": "As Pathfinder, beat the game or obliterate on Monsoon.",
